{
 "manufacturer": "Hitachi",
 "manufacturer_slug": "hitachi",
 "model": "SJ-P1 series inverter (Modbus RTU, firmware Ver. 2.00)",
 "model_slug": "sj-p1",
 "short_model": "Hitachi SJ-P1",
 "aliases": [
  "SJ-P1",
  "P1-xxxxx-L",
  "P1-xxxxx-H"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
 "applies_to": "Hitachi SJ-P1 inverters on the built-in RS485 port in Modbus-RTU mode, register layout of firmware Ver. 2.00 (User's Guide NT251BX-2, Rev. 6).",
 "summary": "The SJ-P1 high-function inverter answers Modbus RTU on its RS485 terminals. Coils carry run/stop, direction, reset and the input/output terminals; holding registers carry the dA/db/dC monitors, trip history, RS485 frequency, torque and PID commands and every parameter. This map lists the control set, main monitors, trip monitor 1 and the CF communication parameters.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "The guide prints register and coil numbers in decimal and hex and says the start number in the frame is the number minus 1; its examples read trip monitor 1 (register 03E9h) with start 03E8h and write coil 1 with start 0000h. So wire address = printed number - 1."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": "Ver. 2.00 register layout (several register numbers differ in Ver. 1.xx)",
 "source": {
  "title": "SJ-P1 Series Inverter User's Guide (chapters 1-20)",
  "doc_number": "NT251BX-2 Rev. 6",
  "revision_date": null,
  "url": "https://www.hitachi-iesa.com/sites/default/files/supportdocs/SJ-P1_Users_guide_chapter1-20_Rev06_NT251BX-2.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 14-5 (CF parameters), 14-11/14-12 (read examples), 14-26 to 14-41 (coil and register lists)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Two-register values are printed as (High) then (Low) register; the guide's read example returns 60.00 Hz as 0000h then 1770h, so the high word comes first (ABCD).",
  "This register layout is for firmware Ver. 2.00. The guide lists items whose register number or range changed from Ver. 1.xx (for example dA-04 was one unsigned register in Ver. 1.xx).",
  "Only a working subset is listed. Later trip monitors repeat the trip monitor 1 block every 20 registers (trip monitor 2 at 1021, 3 at 1041 ...). The full parameter list is in chapter 14.6.",
  "AA101/AA111 are listed without full value tables; the guide states 08 = RS485 for AA101 and 03 = RS485 for AA111. CF-08 (communication method) is left out because its printed codes (00-02) and register range (1-3) disagree.",
  "Monitor and setting ranges assume CF-11 register data selection = 00 (A, V). With 01 (%), current and voltage items read as % of rating.",
  "The single-register input/output power monitors (dA-30, dA-34) are left out: their printed resolution changes with drive size and is given in kWh for a power value."
 ],
